From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: align SM8150 encoder command sequence

Test17 proved that both external queues used bidirectional mappings.
VPU5 accepted SESSION_INIT, internal buffers, LOAD, START and four FTBs.
It also accepted the first ETB. The SoC reset before any EBD or FBD,
disproving DMA direction as the remaining cause.

The complete Xiaomi SM8150 review found two pre-ETB protocol differences.
The generic start path replayed optional controls even when userspace left
them at defaults. Its CAVLC packet also left the CABAC-model word
uninitialized. Buffer counts were also sent as a speculative 4/4 pair at
SESSION_INIT and as another pair at STREAMON. Downstream instead commits
one count from each REQBUFS and queries the final requirements once.

Zero encoder-adjacent packet and property storage. Initialize the entropy
word and leave optional defaults to a fresh firmware session. Retain
non-default standard controls. Commit encoder counts per queue setup and
invalidate the requirement snapshot after a count change. Remove the
speculative pair and use one final requirements query. Also restore the
VPU5 work-mode policy for normal H.264/HEVC, VP8 and CBR low-latency
sessions.

Do not resend the syscache resource on resume: Xiaomi retains its
sys_cache_res_set state across ordinary power collapse. The apparent
resume call is a no-op. Preserve the already-audited DMA directions,
FTB-before-ETB ordering, internal-buffer sequence and power pin. Preserve
the fail-closed encoder gate too.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
